1
00:00:05,848 --> 00:00:07,141
<i>Previously on </i>Reacher...  

2
00:00:07,225 --> 00:00:08,726
[Reacher]<i> Lieutenant Colonel</i> <i>Francis Xavier Quinn.</i>  

3
00:00:08,809 --> 00:00:10,102
[Duffy] <i>You want to find him?</i>  

4
00:00:10,186 --> 00:00:11,771
-[Reacher] <i>Yeah.</i> -[Duffy] <i>So maybe</i> <i>we can help each other out.</i>  

5
00:00:11,854 --> 00:00:14,273
You're gonna get in with Beck by saving his son  

6
00:00:14,357 --> 00:00:16,734
<i>-from getting kidnapped again.</i> -[Reacher] <i>Undercover informant?</i>  

7
00:00:16,817 --> 00:00:18,569
The last one you had went missing.  

8
00:00:18,653 --> 00:00:20,321
[Duffy] <i>So what can I do for you?</i>  

9
00:00:20,404 --> 00:00:23,282
<i>[Reacher] After the fake grenade blasts</i> <i>and a gunfight,</i>  

10
00:00:23,366 --> 00:00:25,159
<i>-Richard won't come with me easily.</i> -[Villanueva] <i>So what do we do?</i>  

11
00:00:25,243 --> 00:00:27,828
We take the option of going to the police completely off the table.  

12
00:00:27,912 --> 00:00:29,789
-[grunts] -You shot a cop!  

13
00:00:29,872 --> 00:00:32,333
<i>-My dad's rich. He can help you.</i> -Mr. Reacher.  

14
00:00:32,416 --> 00:00:35,211
I'm Zachary Beck. I need to see if you can follow orders.  

15
00:00:35,294 --> 00:00:37,046
I'm in.  

16
00:00:37,129 --> 00:00:39,340
<i>-How's the bodyguard?</i> -He's not saying shit.  

17
00:00:39,423 --> 00:00:40,633
[Reacher]<i> Well, I might have</i> <i>a lead on the girl.</i>  

18
00:00:40,716 --> 00:00:42,802
<i>Could've been taken into the carriage</i> <i>house where there's a hidden cellar.</i>  

19
00:00:42,885 --> 00:00:44,929
-[Duffy] <i>Is Teresa there?</i> -No.  

20
00:00:46,222 --> 00:00:47,265
But she was.  

21
00:00:49,141 --> 00:00:51,143
[tense music playing]  

22
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:57,733
[Duffy over phone] <i>I knew</i> <i>Teresa was there.</i>  

23
00:00:57,817 --> 00:00:59,151
<i>Do you see anything else?</i>  

24
00:00:59,235 --> 00:01:00,987
Half-eaten plate of food.  

25
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:04,073
Same one I saw Beck's head of security take out of the house a few hours ago.  

26
00:01:04,156 --> 00:01:06,492
-So Teresa was moved tonight. <i>-We just missed her.</i>  

27
00:01:06,576 --> 00:01:08,703
<i>-She could be somewhere in the house.</i> -No.  

28
00:01:08,786 --> 00:01:10,496
With my arrival and Richard being home now,  

29
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:12,123
there's too much activity on the grounds.  

30
00:01:12,206 --> 00:01:14,333
Too many uncertainties.  

31
00:01:14,417 --> 00:01:16,210
They took her off the property.  

32
00:01:16,294 --> 00:01:17,712
Security cameras?  

33
00:01:17,795 --> 00:01:18,921
From what I saw at the gatehouse,  

34
00:01:19,005 --> 00:01:20,506
eight cameras facing the only road in or out.  

35
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,133
Can you get a look at the footage?  

36
00:01:22,216 --> 00:01:23,676
<i>The film wouldn't show anything.</i>  

37
00:01:23,759 --> 00:01:25,636
Whoever took Teresa would have her in the trunk.  

38
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:27,722
No way to know what car she left in or where they took her  

39
00:01:27,805 --> 00:01:29,599
once she was out of sight of the cameras.  

40
00:01:29,682 --> 00:01:31,100
They could be taking her somewhere to kill her.  

41
00:01:31,183 --> 00:01:32,310
<i>There's no blood in here.</i>  

42
00:01:32,393 --> 00:01:33,728
No sign of any struggle.  

43
00:01:33,811 --> 00:01:36,063
There is a cot, a blanket, a space heater.  

44
00:01:36,147 --> 00:01:38,858
<i>-They fed her.</i> -[sighs] Thank God.  

45
00:01:38,941 --> 00:01:41,485
It's not good news.  

46
00:01:41,569 --> 00:01:45,031
If the people who have her are involved with a guy like Quinn,  

47
00:01:45,114 --> 00:01:48,743
they're not keeping her alive and healthy for a good reason.  

48
00:01:48,826 --> 00:01:51,203
-Fuck. <i>-We'll find her again.</i>  

49
00:01:51,287 --> 00:01:53,831
I got to get back to my room before the rest of the house wakes up.  

50
00:01:53,914 --> 00:01:55,124
Okay.  

51
00:01:56,125 --> 00:01:58,127
[crickets chirping]  

52
00:02:05,509 --> 00:02:07,511
[tense music playing]  

53
00:02:20,232 --> 00:02:22,234
[Duke] What took you so long?  

54
00:02:22,318 --> 00:02:24,654
[speaking indistinctly]  

55
00:02:32,161 --> 00:02:34,163
[Cooper sighing]  

56
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,294
Oh, shit, man. I-I can't sleep in this thing.  

57
00:02:40,378 --> 00:02:41,921
It's fucking uncomfortable.  

58
00:02:42,004 --> 00:02:44,674
-You see me snoring? -Oh. Come on, man.  

59
00:02:44,757 --> 00:02:46,425
I got to some sleep at some point.  

60
00:02:49,345 --> 00:02:51,347
You got the score of the Sox game?  

61
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:54,850
Orioles: five, Red Sox: three.  

62
00:02:54,934 --> 00:02:56,852
Goddamn it.  

63
00:02:56,936 --> 00:02:58,270
[Eliot] Hey, what's up, boss?  

64
00:02:58,354 --> 00:02:59,689
[Duffy] What's Beck doing with Teresa?  

65
00:02:59,772 --> 00:03:00,773
-Oh, fuck. -[Eliot] Hey!  

66
00:03:00,856 --> 00:03:02,775
-You don't want to do this. -Back off! Why are they keeping her?  

67
00:03:02,858 --> 00:03:04,568
-I don't know anything about any Teresa. -[Duffy] Bullshit.  

68
00:03:04,652 --> 00:03:05,820
I know she was there.  

69
00:03:05,903 --> 00:03:07,279
I told you, I'm just a bodyguard.  

70
00:03:07,363 --> 00:03:09,281
I ran your jacket, John Cooper.  

71
00:03:09,365 --> 00:03:10,950
-Fuck. Whatever. -A year for domestic abuse.  

72
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:12,702
Four years, aggravated assault.  

73
00:03:12,785 --> 00:03:14,620
Not someone I'd hire to babysit.  

74
00:03:14,704 --> 00:03:15,871
[spits] Fuck you.  

75
00:03:15,955 --> 00:03:17,748
-Fuck. -What the hell?  

76
00:03:17,832 --> 00:03:19,792
[overlapping shouting]  

77
00:03:19,875 --> 00:03:21,669
-Come on! -[shouting]  

78
00:03:21,752 --> 00:03:23,379
-[Villanueva] Go cool down! -They have Teresa!  

79
00:03:23,462 --> 00:03:25,381
-Go cool down. -They're keeping her prisoner.  

80
00:03:25,464 --> 00:03:27,717
I said step outside and cool down, kid.  

81
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,009
Now.  

82
00:03:30,428 --> 00:03:31,762
[Cooper] Yeah.  

83
00:03:32,847 --> 00:03:34,306
Fuck, man.  

84
00:03:36,726 --> 00:03:39,103
Twelve bucks of coffee, wasted.  

85
00:03:39,186 --> 00:03:41,147
How about you keep a leash on that bitch?  

86
00:03:43,899 --> 00:03:47,570
Call her that again, and I'll leave her alone with you for an hour.  

87
00:03:51,198 --> 00:03:53,325
[laughs softly] Thought so.  

88
00:03:59,457 --> 00:04:01,375
[Duffy] If that piece of shit knows anything--  

89
00:04:01,459 --> 00:04:03,711
That piece of shit is being illegally detained.  

90
00:04:03,794 --> 00:04:07,214
-No, we can claim that we have-- -We can claim my ass is a ham steak,  

91
00:04:07,298 --> 00:04:09,717
but at the end of day, it's just full of shit.  

92
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,136
Look, if we can't pin any of Beck's dirt on him,  

93
00:04:12,219 --> 00:04:15,556
which is a distinct possibility, eventually, we got to set him free,  

94
00:04:15,639 --> 00:04:18,142
and there's gonna be nothing to stop him from singing about all this.  

95
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:20,227
Eh, he won't talk, he's a fucking skell.  

96
00:04:20,311 --> 00:04:21,854
He'll just be happy to be gone.  

97
00:04:21,937 --> 00:04:25,691
Maybe. But if you keep beating his ass, he might carry a beef.  

98
00:04:25,775 --> 00:04:27,526
Then who knows what he does.  

99
00:04:27,610 --> 00:04:29,111
So keep it cool, Susie Q.  

100
00:04:29,195 --> 00:04:31,697
Seriously, Duffy. This-this is already fucked enough.  

101
00:04:31,781 --> 00:04:34,116
I don't want to hear shit from you, Magellan.  

102
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,827
Look, Villy, walk away.  

103
00:04:36,911 --> 00:04:38,454
I don't want you going down with us.  

104
00:04:38,537 --> 00:04:40,122
Not on a favor I pulled you in on.  

105
00:04:40,206 --> 00:04:42,166
Not on something you had nothing to do with.  

106
00:04:42,249 --> 00:04:44,418
Ain't bailing on you now, Irish.  

107
00:04:44,502 --> 00:04:46,629
Just keep the RPMs down.  

108
00:04:50,591 --> 00:04:52,218
Copy that.  

109
00:04:55,012 --> 00:04:58,974
You, get inside and watch the perp.  

110
00:04:59,058 --> 00:05:01,060
Do something useful.  

111
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:10,903
Magellan, huh?  

112
00:05:10,986 --> 00:05:13,489
'Cause he couldn't read the map?  

113
00:05:15,491 --> 00:05:17,535
Sometimes I call him "Ponce de Moron."  

114
00:05:17,618 --> 00:05:20,037
[chuckles]  

115
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,122
Don't go too hard on him.  

116
00:05:22,206 --> 00:05:24,291
He's still part of your team.  

117
00:05:24,375 --> 00:05:26,418
Some team. [scoffs]  

118
00:05:26,502 --> 00:05:31,215
A rookie, an old fart and a gigantic vagrant we barely know.  

119
00:05:31,298 --> 00:05:33,259
And who are you in all of this?  

120
00:05:33,342 --> 00:05:35,761
The idiot who put it all together.  

121
00:05:38,222 --> 00:05:39,723
[groans]  

122
00:05:41,559 --> 00:05:43,435
-[Duke] What do you mean you're not sure if it's there? -[Angel] Well, I-I wasn't there.  

123
00:05:43,519 --> 00:05:45,938
-Can your guy help me? -The big guy inside?  

124
00:05:46,021 --> 00:05:47,731
[Angel] Yeah, can he come with me? He was at the kidnapping.  

125
00:05:47,815 --> 00:05:49,400
[Duke] Come on, I'll get him.  

126
00:05:49,483 --> 00:05:51,360
[Angel] I just want to make sure, you know?  

127
00:05:54,238 --> 00:05:56,031
[Duke] Anything else you want to tell me?  

128
00:05:56,115 --> 00:05:58,117
[speaking indistinctly]  

129
00:05:59,618 --> 00:06:01,620
[suspenseful music playing]  

130
00:06:15,801 --> 00:06:17,720
Wait here.  

131
00:06:17,803 --> 00:06:20,139
Can I go down to the kitchen and grab a drink?  

132
00:06:20,222 --> 00:06:21,891
I don't give a shit.  

133
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,398
[grunts]  

134
00:06:35,779 --> 00:06:37,781
[grunting]  

135
00:06:39,074 --> 00:06:41,076
[panting]  

136
00:06:52,838 --> 00:06:55,633
[grunting]  

137
00:06:57,968 --> 00:06:59,929
[exciting music playing]  

138
00:07:00,012 --> 00:07:01,221
[keys jingle]  

139
00:07:15,861 --> 00:07:17,655
♪ ♪  

140
00:07:27,998 --> 00:07:30,125
[toilet flushes]  

141
00:07:35,297 --> 00:07:36,840
Flattered, but no, thanks.  

142
00:07:36,924 --> 00:07:38,968
Get dressed. There's a job for you.  

143
00:07:39,051 --> 00:07:40,511
At 3:47?  

144
00:07:40,594 --> 00:07:42,429
We found the pickup the kidnappers used.  

145
00:07:42,513 --> 00:07:45,766
Cops took it to some state evidence lot 90 miles south of here.  

146
00:07:45,849 --> 00:07:47,393
There's a guy downstairs. Angel Doll.  

147
00:07:47,476 --> 00:07:50,980
He'll take you to I.D. the truck so we figure out who tried to kidnap Richard.  

148
00:07:51,063 --> 00:07:52,856
Give me five minutes to get dressed.  

149
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,566
You got two.  

150
00:07:57,361 --> 00:07:58,779
[door closes]  

151
00:07:58,862 --> 00:08:00,781
[panting]  

152
00:08:00,864 --> 00:08:02,866
[water running]  

153
00:08:05,869 --> 00:08:07,621
[line ringing]  

154
00:08:07,705 --> 00:08:09,999
-[Duffy over phone] <i>Reacher?</i> -I've got my first job.  

155
00:08:10,082 --> 00:08:12,710
One of Beck's guys is taking me to I.D. the Toyota pickup.  

156
00:08:12,793 --> 00:08:16,380
We made sure all the vehicles involved were sent to a state police impound lot.  

157
00:08:16,463 --> 00:08:17,881
What the hell's their plan for getting in?  

158
00:08:17,965 --> 00:08:21,010
Don't know. I doubt they're gonna just ask nicely.  

159
00:08:21,093 --> 00:08:22,219
Look, I know you said the vehicles  

160
00:08:22,302 --> 00:08:23,804
<i>-won't come back to us, but--</i> -They won't.  

161
00:08:23,887 --> 00:08:26,306
They're all confiscated as government contraband.  

162
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:28,434
If they run any plates, nothing points back to you.  

163
00:08:28,517 --> 00:08:31,270
Did you say all the vehicles went to the same lot?  

164
00:08:31,353 --> 00:08:33,981
-Yeah. Why? <i>-The bodyguard's Audi will be there, too.</i>  

165
00:08:34,064 --> 00:08:35,816
Beck thinks a real grenade went off inside.  

166
00:08:35,899 --> 00:08:38,610
The interior should be covered with blood and brain matter.  

167
00:08:38,694 --> 00:08:41,363
They see a pristine car, the whole kidnapping story falls apart.  

168
00:08:41,447 --> 00:08:43,198
Fuck. Okay.  

169
00:08:43,282 --> 00:08:45,993
I'm gonna head out there and get the Audi off the lot before you show up,  

170
00:08:46,076 --> 00:08:47,286
but you got to buy me time.  

171
00:08:47,369 --> 00:08:48,912
I'll do what I can, but you better move your ass.  

172
00:08:48,996 --> 00:08:50,122
We're leaving now.  

173
00:08:50,205 --> 00:08:52,207
[thunder crashes]  

174
00:09:08,807 --> 00:09:11,351
So, you were a cop in the Army, huh?  

175
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:16,273
Beck had me run your prints.  

176
00:09:16,356 --> 00:09:19,109
What kind of connections you have that you can get your prints processed that fast?  

177
00:09:19,193 --> 00:09:21,070
[laughs] Shit, man.  

178
00:09:21,153 --> 00:09:25,491
I got more hookups than Central Maine Power Company.  

179
00:09:25,574 --> 00:09:27,576
I was in the Army too, you know?  

180
00:09:27,659 --> 00:09:29,912
Until I got thrown out for some bullshit.  

181
00:09:29,995 --> 00:09:31,914
But fuck them, right?  

182
00:09:31,997 --> 00:09:34,458
I make more money now than I ever would have being a grunt.  

183
00:09:35,501 --> 00:09:37,336
Duke called you "Angel Doll."  

184
00:09:37,419 --> 00:09:38,545
Is that really your name?  

185
00:09:38,629 --> 00:09:40,297
Ángel Dole.  

186
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,966
That other shit is just a nickname,  

187
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:46,095
'cause my grandma used to call me her "angel doll"  

188
00:09:46,178 --> 00:09:50,349
after I won the Most Beautiful Baby contest at the county fair.  

189
00:09:50,432 --> 00:09:51,892
It stuck, you know?  

190
00:09:51,975 --> 00:09:54,144
You won?  

191
00:09:54,228 --> 00:09:55,896
Fuck you, man.  

192
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:02,653
I thought Duke was gonna stick me with that <i>pendejo</i> Paulie.  

193
00:10:02,736 --> 00:10:04,738
Always got to play alpha bitch.  

194
00:10:04,822 --> 00:10:06,365
But this is my shit today, man.  

195
00:10:06,448 --> 00:10:09,618
Once we get back, I'm gonna call my ex's Aunt Ginny--  

196
00:10:09,701 --> 00:10:12,746
she works at the DMV-- she'll run the plates for me.  

197
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:15,165
Why would your ex's aunt help you?  

198
00:10:15,249 --> 00:10:18,836
She still loves the shit out of me because we always watched the<i> Wheel </i>together.  

199
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:20,587
Told you, bro.  

200
00:10:20,671 --> 00:10:22,756
More hookups than the power company.  

201
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:25,175
Finding out who went after that kid,  

202
00:10:25,259 --> 00:10:27,302
this is the kind of shit that gets you bumped up, too.  

203
00:10:27,386 --> 00:10:30,889
Even Duke used to do grunt work at the warehouse.  

204
00:10:30,973 --> 00:10:32,558
Look at him now, he's number two,  

205
00:10:32,641 --> 00:10:35,018
living in that big mansion.  

206
00:10:35,102 --> 00:10:36,520
So, Beck promotes from within?  

207
00:10:36,603 --> 00:10:39,690
Who gives a fuck what Zachary Beck thinks?  

208
00:10:39,773 --> 00:10:41,775
[dramatic music playing]  

209
00:10:42,943 --> 00:10:44,987
Who exactly do we work for?  

210
00:10:45,070 --> 00:10:46,196
[laughs]  

211
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:48,407
Got a lot to learn, big fella.  

212
00:10:48,490 --> 00:10:49,992
Got a lot to learn.  

213
00:10:52,911 --> 00:10:54,246
[door opens]  

214
00:10:55,372 --> 00:10:56,832
You in charge?  

215
00:10:56,915 --> 00:10:58,792
[officer] Uh, only one here, so I better be.  

216
00:10:58,876 --> 00:11:01,545
Agents Duffy and Villanueva, DEA.  

217
00:11:01,628 --> 00:11:03,755
Several vehicles were brought in here last night,  

218
00:11:03,839 --> 00:11:05,966
and we need access to one of them. Evidence sweep.  

219
00:11:06,049 --> 00:11:08,468
Uh, yeah, sure.  

220
00:11:08,552 --> 00:11:10,179
-Thanks. Just need a few minutes. -[door buzzes]  

221
00:11:10,262 --> 00:11:12,181
She's got it. I'll wait outside.  

222
00:11:16,351 --> 00:11:18,353
[sighs]  

223
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:21,732
[tense music playing]  

224
00:11:43,378 --> 00:11:44,588
[sighs]  

225
00:11:50,969 --> 00:11:52,763
-[phone beeps] -[line ringing]  

226
00:11:52,846 --> 00:11:54,514
How's it looking?  

227
00:11:54,598 --> 00:11:57,226
Like it's gonna take longer than we thought.  

228
00:11:57,309 --> 00:11:59,603
The Audi's pinned in. I got to move a wreck to get it out.  

229
00:11:59,686 --> 00:12:02,189
Hopefully Reacher's figured out a way to stall.  

230
00:12:02,272 --> 00:12:04,483
-[♪ Rick Coyne: "Had You So Long"] -♪ <i>I know you too damn well</i> ♪  

231
00:12:06,485 --> 00:12:08,362
♪ <i>To let it go </i>♪  

232
00:12:09,780 --> 00:12:12,449
♪ <i>I see your troubled mind </i>♪  

233
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:15,869
♪ <i>Behind your lying eyes </i>♪  

234
00:12:18,872 --> 00:12:20,832
♪ <i>Don't tell me that </i>♪  

235
00:12:20,916 --> 00:12:23,585
-♪ <i>You're still in love with me...</i> -[entry bell dings]  

236
00:12:26,630 --> 00:12:28,215
The fuck you doing, man?  

237
00:12:28,298 --> 00:12:29,716
We got to go.  

238
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,176
Just getting a coffee.  

239
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:33,720
Coffee? So, you just made me stop  

240
00:12:33,804 --> 00:12:36,932
because you said you had to "piss like a racehorse,"  

241
